    "question": {
      ":question/id": "5249685c-c92d-5471-9aed-5dc12f284623",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-15y &=-25 \\\\ 2x-4y &=-4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}5 & -15 & -25 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}5 & -15 & -25 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
