    "question": {
      ":question/id": "4137c00a-560a-5d08-b42e-6c390f1bc83c",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=-19 \\\\ 2x+4y &=12.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -19 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 12\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -19 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -19 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 50\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{10}{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -19 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=-19 \\\\ y &=5,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=5$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-3(5)=-19\\,\u21d2\\,x=-4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-4$ and $y=5.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
